1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:01,740
Mark 10

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:06,940
And he left there, and went to the region of Judea, and beyond the Jordan.

3
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:09,180
And crowds gathered to him again.

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,400
And again, as was his custom, he taught them.

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:16,660
And Pharisees came up, and in order to test him, asked,

6
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:20,040
Is it lawful for a man to divorce his wife?

7
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:21,900
He answered them,

8
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:24,480
What did Moses command you?

9
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:25,880
They said,

10
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:30,720
Moses allowed a man to write a certificate of divorce, and to send her away.

11
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:32,740
And Jesus said to them,

12
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:36,680
Because of your hardness of heart he wrote you this commandment.

13
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:41,400
But from the beginning of creation, God made them male and female.

14
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:46,480
Therefore, a man shall leave his father and mother, and hold fast to his wife,

15
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,840
and the two shall become one flesh.

16
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,660
So they are no longer two, but one flesh.

17
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,940
What therefore God has joined together,

18
00:00:54,940 --> 00:00:57,080
let not man separate.

19
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:01,120
And in the house the disciples asked him again about this matter.

20
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:02,600
And he said to them,

21
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:07,340
Whoever divorces his wife and marries another commits adultery against her.

22
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:11,560
And if she divorces her husband and marries another, she commits adultery.

23
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,980
And they were bringing children to him, that he might touch them.

24
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:16,700
And the disciples rebuked them.

25
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:20,180
But when Jesus saw it, he was indignant and said to them,

26
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:22,440
Let the children come to me.

27
00:01:22,940 --> 00:01:23,960
Do not hinder them.

28
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:24,920
For to say,

29
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:26,800
Such belongs the kingdom of God.

30
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,720
Truly I say to you,

31
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:31,820
Whoever does not receive the kingdom of God like a child,

32
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,320
shall not enter it.

33
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:37,640
And he took them in his arms and blessed them, laying his hands on them.

34
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,340
And as he was setting out on his journey,

35
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:43,120
a man ran up and knelt before him and asked him,

36
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:47,700
Good teacher, what must I do to inherit eternal life?

37
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:50,020
And Jesus said to him,

38
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:52,060
Why do you call me good?

39
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:54,340
No one is good except God alone.

40
00:01:55,100 --> 00:01:56,540
You know the commandments.

41
00:01:57,220 --> 00:01:57,900
Do not murder.

42
00:01:58,340 --> 00:01:59,480
Do not commit adultery.

43
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:00,820
Do not steal.

44
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:02,460
Do not bear false witness.

45
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,240
Do not defraud.

46
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:06,700
Honor your father and mother.

47
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,460
And he said to him,

48
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:12,300
Teacher, all these I have kept from my youth.

49
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:16,460
And Jesus, looking at him, loved him and said to him,

50
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,600
You lack one thing.

51
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:21,920
Go, sell all that you have and give to the poor,

52
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,420
and you will have treasure in heaven.

53
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:24,420
And come forth.

54
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:24,500
And come forth.

55
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:24,520
And come forth.

56
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:24,560
And come forth.

57
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:24,620
And come forth.

58
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:24,680
And come forth.

59
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:24,720
And come forth.

60
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:25,080
And come forth.

61
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:25,100
And come forth.

62
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:25,160
And come forth.

63
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:25,220
And come forth.

64
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:25,260
And come forth.

65
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:25,280
And come forth.

66
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:25,600
Follow me.

67
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:27,800
Disheartened by the saying,

68
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,200
he went away sorrowful,

69
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,720
for he had great possessions.

70
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:34,340
And Jesus looked around and said to his disciples,

71
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,180
How difficult it will be for those who have wealth

72
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:40,080
to enter the kingdom of God.

73
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,360
And the disciples were amazed at his words.

74
00:02:43,820 --> 00:02:45,440
But Jesus said to them again,

75
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:50,000
Children, how difficult it is to enter the kingdom of God.

76
00:02:50,620 --> 00:02:53,880
It is easier for a camel to go through the eye of a needle

77
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,620
than for a rich man to enter the kingdom of God.

78
00:02:54,620 --> 00:03:00,520
a rich person to enter the kingdom of God. And they were exceedingly astonished and said to him,

79
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:08,840
Then who can be saved? Jesus looked at them and said, With man it is impossible, but not with God,

80
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:16,860
for all things are possible with God. Peter began to say to him, See, we have left everything and

81
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:24,020
followed you. Jesus said, Truly I say to you, there is no one who has left house or brothers

82
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:29,220
or sisters or mother or father or children or lands for my sake and for the gospel,

83
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:36,400
who will not receive a hundredfold now in this time, houses and brothers and sisters and mothers

84
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:43,340
and children and lands, with persecutions, and in the age to come eternal life. But many who

85
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:50,760
are first will be last, and the last first. And they were on the road going up to Jerusalem,

86
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:54,000
and Jesus was walking ahead of them. And they were

87
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:59,440
amazed, and those who followed were afraid. And taking the twelve again, he began to tell them

88
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:06,000
what was to happen to him, saying, See, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will

89
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:11,040
be delivered over to the chief priests and the scribes. And they will condemn him to death and

90
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:16,960
deliver him over to the Gentiles. And they will mock him and spit on him and flog him and kill

91
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:23,980
him. And after three days he will rise. And James and John, the sons of Zebedee,

92
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:30,700
came up to him and said to him, Teacher, we want you to do for us whatever we ask of you.

93
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:35,040
And he said to them, What do you want me to do for you?

94
00:04:35,620 --> 00:04:42,160
And they said to him, Grant us to sit one at your right hand and one at your left in your glory.

95
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:46,820
Jesus said to them, You do not know what you are asking.

96
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:52,420
Are you able to drink the cup that I drink, or to be baptized with the baptism with which I am

97
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:52,960
baptized?

98
00:04:54,000 --> 00:05:01,460
said to him, We are able. And Jesus said to them, The cup that I drink you will drink,

99
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:08,160
and with the baptism with which I am baptized you will be baptized. But to sit at my right hand or

100
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:14,520
at my left is not mine to grant, but it is for those for whom it has been prepared. And when

101
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:20,200
the tin heard it, they began to be indignant at James and John. And Jesus called them to him and

102
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:25,380
said to them, You know that those who are considered rulers of the Gentiles lord it over

103
00:05:25,380 --> 00:05:30,860
them, and their great ones exercise authority over them, but it shall not be so among you.

104
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:36,700
But whoever would be great among you must be your servant, and whoever would be first among you must

105
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:43,740
be slave of all. For even the Son of Man came not to be served, but to serve and to give his life

106
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:48,900
as a ransom for many. And they came to Jericho,

107
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,180
and as he was leaving, he saw that there was a man who was in the city of Jericho,

108
00:05:50,180 --> 00:05:55,480
leaving Jericho with his disciples and a great crowd. Bartimaeus, a blind beggar, the son of

109
00:05:55,480 --> 00:06:01,200
Timaeus, was sitting by the roadside. And when he heard that it was Jesus of Nazareth, he began to

110
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:11,680
cry out and say, Jesus, son of David, have mercy on me. And many rebuked him, telling him to be

111
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:19,640
silent. But he cried out all the more, Son of David, have mercy on me.

112
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:26,440
And Jesus stopped and said, Call him. And they called the blind man, saying to him,

113
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:33,560
Take heart, get up, he is calling you. And throwing off his cloak, he sprang up and came

114
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:40,920
to Jesus. And Jesus said to him, What do you want me to do for you? And the blind man said to him,

115
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:49,260
Rabbi, let me recover my sight. And Jesus said to him, Go your way,

116
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:55,520
faith has made you well. And immediately he recovered his sight and followed him on the way.

